 The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 
+## Cached navigation views
+
+The shared layout retains up to five recently visited content views in a
+`transition:persist` main element. Returning to a cached path and query string
+reuses its existing DOM and hydrated islands. Inactive views are hidden and inert,
+and the least recently used views are removed when the cache is full. Hash links
+remain within the same view, and Astro continues to manage history, scroll
+restoration, page titles, and document assets.
+
+Navigation still requests the destination document so the surrounding layout and
+head stay current; this cache saves rebuilding the content view. Cached content
+lasts until eviction or a full reload. Use `cacheView={false}` on `Layout` for
+views that should always be fresh, as the sign-in and sign-up pages do.
+
 ## Tech Stack
 
 - **[Astro](https://astro.build/)**: The web framework for building content-driven websites.
